adjustments:
  getter -= getter-offset
  D *= 94
main loop:
  X += <thing> <- getter is here
  X /= D
  X /= D
  
  Y += X
  Y /= 94
  Y %= 94
  Y += 32
  output char Y
  Y -= Y

  X %= 94
  X += 32
  output char X
  X -= X

  getter += 94 * 24

  Y += getter
  Y == getter-end-of-line check
  time-branch -= Y
  if it's not the end of line:
    back-in-time to main loop

  time-branch += Y
  output newline

  D < 93
  X += D
  X *= 94
  getter += X
  end-of-line-check += X
  getter -= line-reset
  X -= X

  D *= 93
  D += Y
  Y -= Y

  Y += getter
  Y == getter-end-of-file check
  time-jump += Y
  back-in-time to main loop


Variables and constants:
X - the main value being outputteded
Y - temp values and tests
D - divisor, either 94 or 1 depending on the line we're printing
a: 94 - 1 = 93
b: 32
c: 94
d: 24 * 94 = 2256
E: getter-end-of-line check = 1 0 12 2 -1 b
n: newline = 10
f: line-reset = 14 * 24 * 94 = 27072
g: getter-end-of-file-check = 1 4 -2 2 -1 b
h: small back-in-time = 20
i: big back-in-time = 37
j: getter-offset = 2 * 24 * 94


Layout:
--G-- ----- --vE
v---v ----- --<a
|Xjb. dcfgh inDY
>---- ----- --.
